# =============================================================================
# Neptune Local Development Environment — committed, SAFE defaults only
# =============================================================================
# This file is COMMITTED. It must contain no real secrets — only values that
# point at local services or public/dev resources. Real secrets and personal
# overrides go in `.developer.env` (gitignored) or the dev Key Vault; see
# `.developer.env.template`. Layering (later wins):
#   appsettings.json -> appsecrets.json -> Key Vault -> .env -> .developer.env
# =============================================================================

# --- Database (SQL Server in devcontainer) ---
# Local-only SA password: it only secures the throwaway container SQL Server.
DB_SERVER=neptune.db
DB_NAME=NeptuneDB
DB_PASSWORD=DevPassword#1
DB_PORT=8257

# --- Ports ---
# API is plain HTTP. The SPA is served over HTTPS on 8213 with the tracked
# *.localhost.sitkatech.com cert (Neptune.Web/server.crt): Auth0 only has
# https://neptune.localhost.sitkatech.com:8213 registered for local sign-in, so
# any other web port can't log in. Don't run Windows `npm start` at the same time.
API_PORT=8250
WEB_PORT=8213

# --- External service base URLs ---
# Neptune.API builds typed HttpClients from these at request time; an unset one
# 500s every endpoint whose controller injects that client. GDAL / Overlay are
# the docker-compose/ (Visual Studio) stack's services on the host — start them
# there if you need GDB exports or LGU/TGU overlays. There is no local Nereid;
# the placeholder just lets the API start (network solves will fail).
GDALAPIBaseUrl=http://host.docker.internal:8231
OverlayAPIBaseUrl=http://host.docker.internal:8232
OCGISBaseUrl=https://ocgis.com/arcpub/rest/services/
NereidUrl=http://host.docker.internal:8880

# --- ASP.NET Core ---
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development

# --- Azure Key Vault (real-secret source) ---
# The dev vault is read at runtime via DefaultAzureCredential — run `make auth`
# once per host first. Set EMPTY (in .developer.env) to run with no Azure
# dependency; the app then falls back to .env/.developer.env/appsecrets values.
KeyVaultName=neptune-keyvault-dev

# --- Azure CLI auth (for `make auth`, database-download.sh, Key Vault) ---
# Identifiers, not secrets. Tenant-scoping `az login` avoids Conditional-Access
# trips on unrelated tenants; the subscription pin is Managed Services Dev/Test,
# where the neptune dev/qa resources live.
AZURE_TENANT_ID=18ff0aa7-919b-4392-95c6-3b1dcfb1e617
AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=259008ed-0e9b-4dfa-9c7e-c2ca9c5e97ca
AZ_CONTAINER_NAME=prod-backup
AZ_STORAGE_ACCOUNT=neptuneappqa
